le-check: baseline full 1123. After t1 migration (not reflected in baseline? Baseline was before t1? The user ran baseline at 13:33 before changes; t1 was already migrated in repo at that time? Yes t1 e2e existed, baseline 1123 includes 58+3. Then t2 e2e added 62, but old t2 186 still present. So current full if run would be 1185. After deleting old t2: 999. Good.\n\nWait, does adding t2_e2e add 62 discovered tests; yes. 1123+62=1185; minus 186 = 999.\n\nAlso note old t2 tests each 3 ctest entries; removing 62 cases removes 186. Yes.\n\nNow answer concisely.",
