          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Question: principle difference between \"boost::process\" and \"Boost.Process\"? Is one the code namespace and the other the vcpkg package? Answer briefly.\n\nFacts:\n- Boost.Process is the library name (proper noun).\n- `boost::process` is the C++ namespace in code (v1 namespace; with v1 headers it's `boost::process::v1`). In v2 maybe `boost::process` v2. \n- vcpkg port name is `boost-process` (package/port), which brings Boost.Process. Not \"Boost.Process\".\n- So distinction: library name vs namespace vs vcpkg port name. In prose use Boost.Process; in code `boost::process` (and in this project explicitly `boost::process::v1`); in vcpkg manifest `\"boost-process\"`.\n\nKeep short, 3-4 lines. No tools needed. Plan mode, no edits.",
