d. But standard order: Added, Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed, Security. Current Changed→Added→Removed is unconventional but acceptable. [МНЕНИЕ] Can reorder for convention, but not error.\n11. [Unreleased] contains many pre-layer items; fine.\n\nAlso check whether `boost-process` version/port is a \"dependency\" added in this Unreleased cycle; yes, vcpkg.json diff likely from layer 20. Add.\n\nMaybe check git log when vcpkg.json changed; not needed.\n\nAnswer structure:\n- Verdict: general level is fine, README has details; no need to duplicate everything. But 3 bullets have factual issues and two omissions.\n- Fix list:\n  1. Added: add dependency `boost-process` (v1) in vcpkg.json.\n  2. Added line 37: rewrite as sources not .exe; list key artifacts (runner, helper, cases/expected, add_e2e_test, runner self-test).\n  3. Changed line 22: mention t1–t4 and `boost::process::v1`, and that one TEST_P now does 3 checks instead of 3 ctest entries (optional but useful).\n  4. Removed line 44: typo and CTest wording; mention old 3-per-case scheme.\n  5. Optionally mention expectations moved from files to headers.\n- No need to list every file; README covers.\n- Note historical 0.1.0 mentions run_case/check and must stay (history).\n- No blocking errors otherwise.\n\nKeep concise (user asks briefly). No edits.",
